			templ_7745c5c3_Err = templruntime.WriteString(templ_7745c5c3_Buffer, 12, "<h2>“ID checked”</h2><p>The landlord or agent sent us photos of both sides of their Ghana Card and a selfie. A member of our team compared them by hand: the face matches, the card looks genuine, and the name matches the account.</p><p>Landlords with a checked ID publish straight away. Everyone else's listings wait for a moderator to review them first.</p><p>We keep the card photos encrypted and only for as long as we need them: they are deleted 90 days after the decision. The card number is never shown to anyone.</p><h2>“Licensed agent”</h2><p>The agent gave us their licence number and we checked it against the Real Estate Agency Council register. If they sent a certificate, we checked that too.</p><h2>“Owner confirmed”</h2><p>An agent can only list a place with the owner's permission. We text the owner a link; the owner confirms (or says they don't know the agent) without needing an account. Listings where the owner says no, or hasn't confirmed, don't get the badge.</p><h2>“Still available” and freshness</h2><p>Listers are asked regularly to confirm a place is still free. A place that isn't confirmed for 14 days leaves search. If you find one that's already taken, tap “Already rented? Tell us” on the listing and we'll ask the lister.</p><h2>Photos and location</h2><ul><li>We strip hidden data (like GPS) from every photo and look for the same photo on other listings.</li><li>The pin you see is within about 150–400 m of the real place. The exact address is shared only after a lister confirms your viewing.</li><li>Listings close together with matching photos are flagged for a moderator as possible copies.</li></ul><h2>Reliability badges</h2><p>“Replies within a day”, “Reliable for viewings” and “As described” come from what renters actually experienced: how quickly the lister answered viewing requests, whether they turned up, and the feedback after viewings.</p><h2>What a badge doesn't mean</h2><p>Checks lower the risk; they don't remove it. A badge is not a guarantee about the building, the lease or the person. Always view the place in person before you pay, and read our <a href=\"/safety\">safety tips</a>.</p>")
